{
  "format": {
    "about": "Extraction eval cases for the Formal Portal's Requirements Agent (#136, ADR 0040). Each case is one synthetic form submission. scripts/run_extraction_evals.py sends each non-empty list through RequirementsAgent._criteria_to_structured and scores the concepts it returns. This file is a golden file (docs/DAILY_DEV_WORKFLOW.md section 7): never fill an expected value from model output.",
    "cases[].id": "Stable case id, used in the JSONL evidence.",
    "cases[].signoff": "Who approved the expected values, and when. The loader rejects the file if a case has none.",
    "cases[].inclusion": "Inclusion criteria: a list of {criterion, expected}.",
    "cases[].exclusion": "Optional exclusion criteria, same shape. Here an expected polarity of has also matches a concept marked excluded, because the list already negates it (ADR 0036).",
    "criterion": "The criterion text a researcher submits. Synthetic phrasings only.",
    "expected": "Every concept the criterion must extract. A case passes when each criterion returns exactly these concepts, with no extras.",
    "expected[] condition | medication | procedure | lab": "{type, terms, polarity}. terms lists the accepted terms; the extracted term must equal one after lowercasing and collapsing whitespace. polarity is has, excluded (the details hold the word excluded) or family_history (SQLGenerator's family-history pattern matches a condition's term and details).",
    "expected[] demographic age": "{type: demographic, age: [op, value]}, compared with SQLGenerator._parse_age_details: [\">\", 65], [\">=\", 65], [\"BETWEEN\", [50, 60]].",
    "expected[] demographic gender": "{type: demographic, gender: female | male}, compared with SQLGenerator's gender rule.",
    "expected[].temporal_within": "Optional [N, unit], such as [6, \"months\"]. Reported per case; it doesn't affect pass or fail.",
    "not scored": "Concept codes (always empty until a terminology step exists, #154) and lab value thresholds (no consumer reads them).",
    "expected[] demographic age, two bounds": "[\"AND\", [[lower_op, n], [upper_op, m]]] or [\"OR\", [[upper_op, n], [lower_op, m]]], in the order _parse_age_details returns them.",
    "how to add a case": "1. Write the criteria in a synthetic phrasing and the expected concepts by hand, never from model output. 2. Get the owner's approval and put it in signoff. 3. Add a correct hand-written extraction for each new criterion to tests/eval/test_extraction_evals.py, so a test shows the expectation can be met. 4. Re-baseline (below): the CI replay fails on any request the recording lacks, so a new case can't merge without one.",
    "how to re-baseline": "Needed after any change to this file, the extraction prompt or the model (ADR 0041). Each live run is billed, so get the owner's OK first. Commit the change first, so the recording names a commit that holds it rather than one marked -dirty. Run: .venv/bin/python -m scripts.run_extraction_evals --repeat 5 --record. Run 1 becomes tests/eval/fixtures/extraction_recording.json, written only if all five runs are trusted. Set --fail-under in the CI step (.github/workflows/tests.yml) to the lowest pass rate the runner prints, and --min-cases to the number of cases here. The threshold goes up only. Lowering it needs the owner's OK and a line under Changed expectations in the PR body."
  },
